      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T19:11:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You didn\u0027t change this, but this rule makes every host utility depend on the entire set of host source files (host-srcs). This means that changing a source file for one tool (e.g., ectool.cc) will trigger a relink/rebuild check for all other host tools. While the cmd_c_to_host logic correctly identifies the specific objects to compile, the broad dependency list at the Make level causes unnecessary overhead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "2e055f98d247ceaf52a4466ff950fd0e30750c36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "787d177b_ba85a7c0",
        "filename": "Makefile.rules",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 127,
      "author": {
        "id": 1483403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T19:11:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the removal of the firmware object rules, the order-only dependency on ec_version.h (previously at lines 170-171) is gone. Host tools like ectool include ec_version.h, and in a clean parallel build, the compilation might start before ec_version.h is generated, leading to a build failure.\n\nConsider adding an order-only dependency here:\n$(host-utils) $(host-utils-cxx): | $(out)/ec_version.h",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 0
      },
